<title>SWEDEN: Sweden to stick to currency policy - Asbrink.</title>
<headline>Sweden to stick to currency policy - Asbrink.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-10-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish Finance Minister Erik Asbrink said Finland's adhesion to the EU's Exchange Rate Mechanism (ERM) did not affect Sweden and there was no reason to change Sweden's monetary and currency policies.  </p>
<p>Asbrink said in a statement that Sweden and Finland had taken their own positions on the question of the ERM and EMU (economic and monetary union).</p>
<p>&quot;Finland's decision to adhere to the ERM does not affect Sweden's view. It is the government's view that it is not on the agenda for Sweden to link the crown to the ERM.</p>
<p>&quot;Price stability is the overwhelming goal of monetary policy. This direction for monetary and currency policy has been successful and there is no reason to change it,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>-- Simon Haydon, Stockholm newsroom, 46 8 753 6189</p>
</text>
